      <workList xml:id="workDesc_eb474291">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e223220">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_9936b870">B4:006</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="la">Sanctus</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_e7e247ce">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_20">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_21_0">
               <date isodate="1731-12-30" xml:id="date_55cfa098">30 December 1731</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_21_0">Leipzig,</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_21_0">
               <p xml:id="idm241">Among the works that Scheibe composed during his early years in Leipzig are a few Magnificats and Sanctus sections of which the present one is dated 30 December 1731 by Scheibe. It was most likely commissioned by the cantor of Neukirche, <persName xml:id="idm242" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Carl Gotthelf Gerlach</persName>, and was performed sometime during the beginning of 1732. In 1761 it was acquired by Breitkopf from the Gerlach estate as it is listed in their catalogue of that year as one of their master copies. Scheibe does not seem to have composed many Sanctus settings which often were played during communion.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_05be6eb2">
